{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1969","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Card Pairing"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a deck of $$$n$$$ cards, each card has one of $$$k$$$ types. You are given the sequence $$$a_1, a_2, \\dots, a_n$$$ denoting the types of cards in the deck from top to bottom. Both $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ are even numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You play a game with these cards. First, you draw $$$k$$$ topmost cards from the deck. Then, the following happens each turn of the game:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" you choose "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" two cards from your hand and play them. If these cards have the same type, you earn a coin; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" then, if the deck is not empty, you draw "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" two top cards from it; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" then, if both your hand and your deck are empty, the game ends. Otherwise, the new turn begins. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to calculate the maximum number of coins you can earn during the game."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs